  "notes": "Camellia Plc (AIM, GBP reporting). Diversified ag conglomerate: Tea (Kenya, Malawi, Bangladesh, India), Avocado (Kenya), Macadamia (Malawi/South Africa), Engineering (AKD UK), Investments. UK semi-annual reporter (H1 interim June + FY December). Tea remains largest segment by revenue (~55%); macadamia and avocado materially smaller but growing. ~50,000 ha total ag area (~124k acres). Camellia disposed of legacy investments and food-services operations 2022-2024 to refocus on agriculture; FY24 revenue reflects continuing operations only. Segment splits drawn from annual-report Note 4 (operating segments). Historical FY 1995-2019 from archived annual reports / Companies House filings (annual report archive on IR site goes back to 1996; 1995 from Companies House); pre-2002 figures reflect Linton Park Plc-era reporting (renamed Camellia 2003). Group has owned tea estates since the 1880s; modern conglomerate structure dating from 1980s acquisition trail (Goodricke, Eastern Produce, Bordon, AKD, etc.). H1 interim cadence began consistently from 2003; pre-2003 only annual figures available. Engineering / food-services included historically; refocus to agri-only is 2022-2024. Operating expense breakdown (Cost of sales / Distribution costs / Administrative expenses) drawn from consolidated income statement of Camellia Plc / Linton Park Plc annual reports filed on camellia.plc.uk IR archive (2002+) and Companies House (pre-2002). H1 interims summarize and do not split distribution costs out, so field omitted there.",
